.DS_Store
.env*
!.env.example
*.notes.md
localstorage.json
.notes/
node_modules/
build/
/world*
# python bytecode from the roomsrc install scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Tripo pipeline output. The finished avatars are tracked — they are what
# makes a fresh clone playable, and thinned down they are a couple of MB each.
# The intermediates are not: they are ten times the size and regenerable.
roomsrc/cast_vrm/*
!roomsrc/cast_vrm/*.vrm

# Deploy secrets, written on the server by deploy/setup.sh. Ignored before
# anything writes here, so the admin code cannot reach a public repo.
deploy/secrets/

# Generated props. The finished models are tracked — they are what the world
# places. The raw downloads are ten to fifteen MB each and regenerable, and
# state.json is task ids, not source.
roomsrc/props/*_raw.glb
roomsrc/props/state.json

# Fetched CC0 packs. Not committed — 31MB of someone else's assets, and
# fetch_packs.py pulls them on demand. The script is the source of truth.
roomsrc/packs/
# Poly Haven photoscans. The 188MB of raw downloads stay out; the 11MB of
# decimated ones are committed, because they are the only geometry in the world
# carrying a normal map and a deploy that quietly loses them looks like the
# cartoon build we just left. CC0, so redistributing them is fine.
roomsrc/hq/*.raw.glb

# Poly Haven texture downloads. fetch_tex.py re-pulls them and bakes the
# tiled sheets beside them; only the sheets are worth keeping.
roomsrc/tex/raw/
